# Visual Statistical Analysis

## lauching Packages


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
pacman::p_load(ggstatsplot, tidyverse)
```
:::


## Importing Data


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
exam <- read_csv("/Users/zhanyi/Desktop/M Y1S2/ISSS608/ISSS608-VAA/project 1/ISSS608/Hands-on_Ex/Hands-on_Ex04b/data/Exam_data.csv")
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
exam$MATHS <- as.numeric(exam$MATHS)
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
exam$ENGLISH <- as.numeric(exam$ENGLISH)
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
exam$SCIENCE <- as.numeric(exam$SCIENCE)
```
:::


### One-sample test: gghistostats() method


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
set.seed(1234)

gghistostats(
  data = exam,
  x = ENGLISH,
  type = "bayes",
  test.value = 60,
  xlab = "English scores"
)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex04b_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-6-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Two-sample mean test: ggbetweenstats()


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggbetweenstats(
  data = exam,
  x = GENDER, 
  y = MATHS,
  type = "np",
  messages = FALSE
)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex04b_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-7-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Oneway ANOVA Test: ggbetweenstats() method


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggbetweenstats(
  data = exam,
  x = RACE, 
  y = ENGLISH,
  type = "p",
  mean.ci = TRUE, 
  pairwise.comparisons = TRUE, 
  pairwise.display = "s",
  p.adjust.method = "fdr",
  messages = FALSE
)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex04b_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-8-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Significant Test of Correlation: ggscatterstats()


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggscatterstats(
  data = exam,
  x = MATHS,
  y = ENGLISH,
  marginal = FALSE,
  )
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex04b_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-9-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::


### Significant Test of Association (Depedence) : ggbarstats() methods


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
exam1 <- exam %>% 
  mutate(MATHS_bins = 
           cut(MATHS, 
               breaks = c(0,60,75,85,100))
)
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
ggbarstats(exam1, 
           x = MATHS_bins, 
           y = GENDER)
```

::: {.cell-output-display}
![](Hands-on_Ex04b_files/figure-html/unnamed-chunk-11-1.png){width=672}
:::
:::
